    "collection-faq": {
      "type": "collection-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "f1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the Outdoor Performance Skin actually for?",
            "answer": "<p>Outdoor volleyball. Outdoor yoga. Resortwear &amp; travel. Sun-baked pavement. Anywhere you'd go barefoot, but better.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are they better than going barefoot?",
            "answer": "<p>For many people, yes. The heel and sole are covered and the grip holds where bare feet slip. Your toes stay open, so you keep the barefoot feel.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f4": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is there any surface I should be mindful of?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Like any footwear, Barreletics won’t create grip where a surface has none.</p><p>Wet tile, wet stone, and other slick floors are inherently slippery for any footwear. Always check the surface before you trust it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f5": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I clean them?",
            "answer": "<p>Hand wash with warm soapy water. That's it.</p><p>How to put on: pull from the top of the foot, not the straps, to help extend their lifespan.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f6": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What size should I order?",
            "answer": "<p>Your usual shoe size is the place to start. Expect a snug, second-skin fit with no break-in. If your feet are narrow or wide, your size may change, so check the <a href=\"/pages/performance-skins-size-chart\">size guide</a> before ordering.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long will they last?",
            "answer": "<p>Heel and sole covered, toes open. For everywhere you'd usually go barefoot but want a little grip and protection: rocky beaches and shorelines, hot sand, pool decks, paddle-boards, docks and boat decks, lake days, and hotel and resort walkways.<br/><br/>Like any footwear, Barreletics won't create grip where a surface has none. Wet tile, wet stone, and other slick floors are inherently slippery for any footwear. Always check the surface before you trust it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "f8": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's the return and warranty policy?",
            "answer": "<p>30 days to return or exchange, and a 90-day warranty against manufacturing defects. Read the full policy on our <a href=\"/pages/returns\">returns page</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "geo-beach": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Grippy shoes for hot sand and pavement",
            "answer": "<p>For places you might otherwise go barefoot, like hot sand or sun-baked pavement. A barrier where it matters: the sole creates just enough separation to keep you comfortable without losing ground feel.</p>"
          }
        },
        "geo-boat": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Grippy shoes for boat decks",
            "answer": "<p>If you would otherwise go barefoot on a boat deck, Barreletics cover your heel and sole and give you grip where bare feet slip. For slick surfaces, see <em>Good to know</em> above and “Is there any surface I should be mindful of?”</p>"
          }
        },
        "geo-travel": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Packable grippy shoes for travel and resortwear",
            "answer": "<p>Resortwear &amp; travel. Travel-friendly, zero maintenance: rinse and go. Whether practicing at home or on the go, travel light and workout without having a yoga mat in tow.</p>"
          }
        },
        "geo-outdoor-yoga": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Grip footwear for outdoor yoga",
            "answer": "<p>Outdoor yoga. Outdoor volleyball: grip on sand and grass without bulk. The open-toe design lets your toes spread naturally, giving you better balance, better grip, and a more connected feel underfoot.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
